TITAN XDR/XTC reader provenance

The original xdrfile.cpp, xdrfile_xtc.cpp, and xdrfile_trr.cpp files in this
directory come from the standalone GROMACS xdrfile code path with the
2009-2014 BSD-style notice preserved in each source file.

TITAN's modern XTC compatibility updates for magic 2023, 64-bit compressed
payload byte counts, and the float-coordinate DataBuffer/receivebits/
receiveints decoder were derived from the GROMACS 2026.3 xdr3dfcoord reader:

- D:\data_MD\gromacs-2026.3\src\gromacs\fileio\xdrf.h
- D:\data_MD\gromacs-2026.3\src\gromacs\fileio\libxdrf.cpp
- D:\data_MD\gromacs-2026.3\src\gromacs\fileio\xtcio.cpp

Those GROMACS files are licensed under LGPL-2.1-or-later by the GROMACS
authors. Keep this note with any redistribution of TITAN builds that include
the modernized XTC reader, and include the corresponding GROMACS/TITAN source
for the modified reader component when distributing binaries.
